.TH TUIDESK\-LUA 7 2026-10-27 "tuidesk 0.1.0" "Miscellaneous"
.SH NAME
tuidesk\-lua \- Lua plugin interface of tuidesk
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/init.lua
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tuidesk (1)
runs
.I init.lua
in Lua 5.4 when it starts, and again whenever the file is saved.
Modules in
.I ~/.config/tuidesk/lua/
can be loaded with
.BR require .
The interface is the global table
.BR tuidesk .
.PP
Errors are shown as notifications.
Each call into Lua may run for 2 seconds before it is stopped, and actions started from Lua
may nest 4 levels deep, so a faulty script cannot freeze or crash the desktop.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BI tuidesk.notify( title " [, " body " [, " seconds "]])"
Show a notification.
.TP
.BI tuidesk.spawn( command )
Open a window running
.I command
through
.BR /bin/sh .
.TP
.BI tuidesk.action( name )
Run a key binding action, such as
.B \(dqmaximize\(dq
or
.BR "\(dqdesktop 2\(dq" ;
see
.BR tuidesk\-config (5).
.TP
.BI tuidesk.bind( key ", " function )
A direct key binding, such as
.BR \(dqalt+g\(dq .
.TP
.BI tuidesk.bind_prefix( key ", " function )
A binding used after the prefix key.
.TP
.BI tuidesk.on( event ", " function )
Call
.I function
on an event; see
.BR EVENTS .
.TP
.BI tuidesk.widget( name ", " function " [, " seconds "])"
Register a widget whose text is
.IR function 's
result, refreshed every
.I seconds
(default 1, at least 0.2).
Show it in the panel by adding
.BI \(dqlua: name \(dq
to
.BR panel.widgets ,
or on the desktop as a
.B lua
wallpaper or desktop widget.
.TP
.BI tuidesk.rule{ ... }
Add a window rule, with the keys of
.B [[rules]]
in
.BR tuidesk\-config (5):
.BR command ,
.BR title ,
.BR width ,
.BR height ,
.BR x ,
.BR y ,
.BR maximized ,
.BR minimized ,
.BR floating ,
.BR above ,
.BR desktop .
.TP
.B tuidesk.windows()
A list of window tables.
.TP
.BI tuidesk.focus( id "), tuidesk.close(" id )
Focus or close a window.
.SH EVENTS
.TP 14
.B startup
Once, after the session is restored.
.TP
.B tick
Every second.
.TP
.BR window_open ", " window_close
A window opened or closed; the handler receives its window table.
.TP
.B focus
Another window got the focus; the handler receives its window table.
.SH WINDOW TABLES
.TP 12
.B id
Number used by
.BR tuidesk.focus ,
.B tuidesk.close
and
.BR "tuidesk msg" .
.TP
.BR title ", " command
The window's title and command.
.TP
.BR focused ", " minimized
Booleans.
.TP
.B desktop
The desktop the window is on.
.TP
.B exit_code
The program's exit status, in
.B window_close
handlers.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open lazygit maximized with the prefix key, then
.BR g :
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk.bind_prefix("g", function()
  tuidesk.spawn("lazygit")
end)
tuidesk.rule { command = "lazygit", maximized = true }
.fi
.RE
.PP
A load average panel widget, shown by adding
.B \(dqlua:load\(dq
to
.BR panel.widgets :
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk.widget("load", function()
  local f = io.popen("cut \-d\(aq \(aq \-f1\-3 /proc/loadavg")
  local out = f:read("*l") or ""
  f:close()
  return "load " .. out
end, 5)
.fi
.RE
.PP
Report programs that exit with an error:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tuidesk.on("window_close", function(win)
  if win.exit_code and win.exit_code \(ti= 0 then
    tuidesk.notify(win.title, "exited with code " .. win.exit_code)
  end
end)
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tuidesk (1),
.BR tuidesk\-config (5),
.BR lua (1)
